# Supply-chain cooldown: `npm install <pkg>` and `npm update` only resolve versions published
# more than 3 days ago, transitive ones included, so a freshly hijacked release has time to be
# caught and yanked before it can land here. `npm ci` installs package-lock.json exactly as
# written and ignores this. Dependabot's `cooldown` in .github/dependabot.yml matches it.
#
# Side effects while anything in the tree is under 3 days old (both fail closed with ETARGET):
#   - `npm update`, when a package.json range's floor is itself that new: wait it out;
#   - `npm audit signatures`, which applies the same filter to locked versions: run it with
#     `--min-release-age=0`. Plain `npm audit` and `npm ci` are unaffected.
# Urgent security fix that can't wait: bypass the policy once, for that package only:
#   npm install <pkg>@<fixed-version> --min-release-age=0
min-release-age=3
